  "scenario_narratives": {
    "base": "Allianz delivers roughly its own plan: operating profit at the guided ~EUR 17.4bn in 2026 then mid-single-digit growth, P&C combined ratio held at 92-93%, L/H CSM release 8-9%, PIMCO/AllianzGI margins under passive pressure but flows positive. Core NI compounds ~4% in aggregate (7-8% per share with buy-backs) fading to 3%, with ~80% paid out. Cost of equity 8.5%.",
    "bull": "Pricing and productivity (AI, Allianz Direct, claims automation) push P&C combined ratio toward 91%, higher-for-longer rates lift the operating investment result and L/H new business (VNB EUR 4.8bn), and asset management returns to inflows. Core NI grows 7% near term (upper half of the 7-9% EPS target before buy-back accretion), payout 82%, and the market re-rates a 218%-solvency AA franchise toward a 7.75% cost of equity.",
    "bear": "A heavy nat-cat year (guidance assumes ~3% of NEP vs 1.4% in 2025) plus an equity/credit drawdown and a USD weakening (10% USD move is disclosed as material) cut 2026 core NI 3%; the Solvency II ratio falls toward the high-100s and buy-backs are trimmed to the 15% floor (payout 75%). PIMCO fee compression continues. Recovery to 2-3% growth; cost of equity 9.5%, terminal growth 2%."
  },
  "valuation_philosophy": {
    "summary": "Allianz is valued on what it can distribute to shareholders: core net income times a payout ratio set by its Capital Management Policy (60% dividend + >=15% buy-backs), discounted at a EUR cost of equity with no net-debt deduction. Owner FCF, EBITDA and net debt have no meaning for an insurer. Justified P/B on core RoE is the cross-check.",
    "key_risks_to_valuation": [
      "Nat-cat severity above the ~3% of NEP budget (climate-driven frequency, U.S. and European convective storms).",
      "Capital-market drawdown: equity/credit/spread shocks hit the Solvency II ratio and could pause buy-backs; distributions are discretionary.",
      "Asset management fee compression at PIMCO and AllianzGI from passive products; outflows in a bond bear market.",
      "USD/EUR translation: guidance assumes 1.17; a 10% USD move is disclosed as material to operating profit.",
      "Cost-of-equity sensitivity: each 50bp on CoE moves the base value ~10%.",
      "Litigation tail (Structured Alpha precedent) and regulatory interference (German/EU tax, Solvency II review)."
    ]
  },
