    "notes": "MODEL: insurer -> FCFE at cost of equity via the component engine with net debt held at zero, following the house precedent for insurers (PRU, MET, GL, IAG.AX, LGEN.L). The skill's routing table lists 'BVPS compounding x exit P/B' for insurers; that is used here as a cross-check rather than the primary because IFRS 17 (FY2023) broke the equity series (FY2020 EUR 80.8bn IFRS 4 vs FY2025 EUR 62.7bn) and equity excludes the EUR 55.9bn CSM, so book is not where the value sits. ENGINE MAPPING: base_revenue = shareholders' core net income; ebitda_margin_path = total payout ratio (dividend + buy-back as % of core NI); SBC, D&A, capex, cash tax, lease and working capital set to zero because core NI is already post-tax, post-interest and post-SBC. Flow = distributable FCFE; discounted at cost of equity; net_debt = 0 (financial debt is operating funding of an insurer and is already charged in core NI; subtracting it again would double-count). CROSS-CHECK: BVPS EUR 165 (62,722 / 380.2), core RoE 18.1% -> justified P/B (RoE - g)/(CoE - g) = (18 - 3.5)/(8.5 - 3.5) = 2.9x -> ~EUR 480, vs market P/B 2.6x. Analysis JSON was not yet available at build time (concurrent agent); qualitative inputs taken from the FY2025 annual report outlook and the Q3-2025 presentation. No H1-2026 interim is extracted, so FY2026 is judged from guidance only.",
